It's really simple. 
I've made this one line change.
```
diff --git a/src/nvim/syntax.c b/src/nvim/syntax.c
index 913fd0548..efc60b746 100644
--- a/src/nvim/syntax.c
+++ b/src/nvim/syntax.c
@@ -6647,7 +6647,7 @@ do_highlight(char_u *line, int forceit, int init) {
   if (error && idx == highlight_ga.ga_len) {
     syn_unadd_group();
   } else {
-    if (is_normal_group) {
+    if (!error && is_normal_group) {
       // Need to update all groups, because they might be using "bg" and/or
       // "fg", which have been changed now.
       highlight_attr_set_all();
```
So, let me know if this is correct and want me to do a PR or not.
I'm don't understand it very well to see conflicts. Hopefully you can tell @justinmk .
